// Multiple articulations on ONE note stack outward in LilyPond script-priority
// order — staccato innermost, then default scripts (accent/marcato), then the
// written order for ties — regardless of the order they were written. The
// second note writes them scrambled (tenuto, marcato, staccato) to prove the
// sort reorders to staccato-innermost. Guards ArticulationEngraver's per-note
// script stacking; they used to overprint at the same Y.
// LILYPOND-REF: scm/script.scm script-priority (staccato -100, tenuto -50).
title "Script stacking"
octave absolute
time 4/4
key c major

part melody

phrase stack {
  g'4@staccato@accent@marcato c''4@tenuto@marcato@staccato e'4@accent@staccato r4 |
}

section Main { melody { stack } }
form main { Main }
score main "script-stacking" {
  staff melody
}

